---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import VideoSlot from '../../components/VideoSlot.astro';
---

<GuideLayout
  title="The screens"
  tag="Guide"
  description="What each part of the app shows, and when it's worth opening."
>
  <section class="section">
    <h2>Watch it first</h2>
    <p>A quick tour of the app after a few rounds are logged.</p>
    <VideoSlot title="A tour of The Yips screens" />
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>The bottom bar</h2>
    <p>
      Four tabs: <span class="ui">Rounds</span>, <span class="ui">Bag</span>,
      <span class="ui">Trends</span>, and <span class="ui">Stats</span>. Settings
      lives behind the gear on the Rounds screen.
    </p>

    <h3>Rounds</h3>
    <p>
      Your recent rounds, your career averages, and your handicap badge.
      Tap <span class="ui">New round</span> to start one, or tap a past round
      to open its detail. A round in progress is pinned here, with a shortcut
      to resume it.
    </p>

    <h3>Round detail</h3>
    <p>
      The full picture of one round: scorecard, stats grid, scoring breakdown,
      and the highlights (eagles through doubles, up and downs, sand saves).
      The Yips will also have an opinion about how you played. Brace yourself.
    </p>

    <h3>Bag</h3>
    <p>
      Your clubs, which ones are in the bag, and the average distance for
      each. Tap a club for its history. Averages use your good shots only, so
      you see what the club does when you hit it well, and a club needs 5 good
      shots before outliers are trimmed.
    </p>
    <p>
      Wedge averages include chips and pitches, so they'll read shorter than
      your full-swing distance. Tap a club to see its individual shots.
    </p>

    <h3>Trends</h3>
    <p>
      Charts over time, and the way into the deeper views below. This is the
      place to spot a pattern across rounds, not just in the last one.
    </p>

    <h3>Stats</h3>
    <p>
      Career numbers: scoring distribution, putts, penalties, and the classics
      like fairways and greens in regulation. See
      <a href="/stats" class="ui">how stats work</a> for what each one means.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>The deeper views</h2>
    <p>Open these from <span class="ui">Trends</span>.</p>

    <h3>Strokes Gained</h3>
    <p>
      Where your strokes went, split into Off the Tee, Approach, Around the
      Green, and Putting, compared against the handicap level you pick in
      Settings. A negative number isn't a failure. It's where the strokes are.
    </p>

    <h3>Putting</h3>
    <p>How many putts you take, broken down by first-putt distance.</p>

    <h3>Tee shots</h3>
    <p>Fairways hit, which way you miss, and how each tee shot sets up the hole.</p>

    <h3>Club performance</h3>
    <p>
      How each club is really performing: distances, how often your shots are
      good, and which club is overdue for some practice.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Settings</h2>
    <p>
      Theme, on-course options, your account and sync, the Strokes Gained
      benchmark level, privacy options, and feedback. If something about the
      app isn't the way you want it, look here first.
    </p>
  </section>
</GuideLayout>
